{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_014fyFQMyRaPNWPjhEpfxYXx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dvt5JUEWwvvVe411A1MXWa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /src/mxfs; sed -n '60,140p' SUCCESS_CRITERIA.md","description":"Read rest of success criteria"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5851,"cache_read_input_tokens":43236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5851},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd05e5a4-1bae-4b40-b8b4-ee58800ac150","uuid":"73ef3c28-54b3-4dc9-bbe8-15bd64fb06ab","request_id":"req_011CbvkmsjtiC2Ry62j3AhW6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dvt5JUEWwvvVe411A1MXWa","type":"tool_result","content":"## Persistent state: `.criteria_results.json`\n\nThe repo holds a `.criteria_results.json` at its root.  Every\ncriterion script writes/updates its entry there on every run.  The\nschema is:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mkfs_timing\":     { \"status\": \"PASS\", \"last_run_iso\": \"...\", \"measured\": \"639ms\", \"threshold\": \"<=10000ms\", \"reason\": \"\" },\n  \"zero_silent_loss\":{ \"status\": \"FAIL\", \"last_run_iso\": \"...\", \"measured\": \"...\", \"threshold\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\" }\n}\n```\n\nThis is the model's **source of truth across sessions**.  On a fresh\nsession, before doing anything, run:\n\n```bash\n./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh --status\n```\n\nThis prints the current state of every criterion (from the JSON\nfile) without re-running anything.  Use it to:\n\n- See what's currently failing.\n- Pick the next failing criterion to work on.\n- Avoid re-running already-passing criteria mid-iteration.\n\nWhen a criterion script runs, it overwrites its own entry — so the\nfile always reflects each criterion's most-recent run.\n\n**Important:** `--status` shows the *last* result per criterion, which\nmay come from different runs.  The ship gate requires all criteria\nPASS in ONE end-to-end `verify_ship.sh` run (step 4 above).\n\n## Threshold rule\n\nThresholds reflect what the workload *should* take given the\narchitecture, not arbitrary caps.  If single-node rsync is 4s, 2-node\nparallel rsync should be ≈ 4s ± small constant.  If a verifier\nroutinely fails because the work is much slower than expected, fix\nthe FS — don't widen the threshold.\n\nCommon args for every verifier: `--nodes N` (count or comma list of\nhostnames), `--module PATH`, `--device DEV`, `--mount PATH`.  Defaults\ntarget the test17-test32 / `/dev/sda` / `/mnt/shared` cluster.\n\n---\n\n## CORRECTNESS (non-negotiable)\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| POSIX semantics preserved on every operation, from every node, under every concurrency pattern. | `tests/criteria/posix_semantics.sh --nodes 16` |\n| Zero silent data loss and zero silent dirent loss under any workload. | `tests/criteria/zero_silent_loss.sh --iters 3 --dpn 100 --mode 1` |\n| Crash consistency: acknowledged writes (post-fsync, post-close) survive any node death or power loss. | `tests/criteria/crash_consistency.sh --nodes 2` |\n| Cluster membership changes (join, leave, fence, recover) cannot lose data. | `tests/criteria/fence_during_write.sh --nodes 4` |\n| No false ENOENT/EEXIST under concurrent access — cache coherency is correct. | `tests/criteria/cache_coherency.sh --nodes 4` |\n| Strong consistency for fsync'd writes across nodes: a reader on node B sees them as soon as writer on node A's fsync returns. | `tests/criteria/strong_consistency.sh --nodes 4` |\n\n## SCALE\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| 16-node concurrent active R/W mount as the baseline target. | `tests/criteria/posix_semantics.sh --nodes 16` (covers it; cluster phase requires all 16 mounted) |\n| Surviving nodes continue uninterrupted after any single-node fence or death; automatic journal replay. | `tests/criteria/fence_during_write.sh --nodes 4` |\n| Workload doesn't degrade pathologically as nodes are added (no quadratic-cost ops). | `tests/criteria/scaling_curve.sh --nodes 16` |\n\n## PERFORMANCE — must be near-native XFS\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| Single-node mxfs operations within **≤ 5%** of native XFS on the same LUN (rsync as the canonical workload). | `tests/criteria/single_node_paired.sh --nodes 1` |\n| N-node aggregate throughput scales with N for embarrassingly-parallel workloads (independent files/dirs across nodes). | `tests/criteria/scaling_curve.sh --nodes 16` |\n| Canonical N-node rsync bench: per-node mxfs wall ≤ 1.2× single-node XFS reference. | `tests/criteria/rsync_paired.sh --nodes 4 --iters 1` |\n| Cluster ops (mount, unmount) complete in **seconds**, not minutes. | `tests/criteria/cluster_ops_timing.sh --nodes 4` |\n| No routine workload takes >2× the single-node XFS time. | Covered by `single_node_paired.sh` (single) and `rsync_paired.sh` (multi-node). |\n\n**Removed bullet:** \"Shared-resource contention within an order of\nmagnitude of GFS2/OCFS2.\"  We have no apples-to-apples GFS2/OCFS2\ntestbed here.  Shared-dir contention is instead bounded by\n`zero_silent_loss.sh`'s wall ceiling — any per-iter wall > a few","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd05e5a4-1bae-4b40-b8b4-ee58800ac150","uuid":"9b815cc2-52f8-4f4c-b1a3-40906d4a9882","timestamp":"2026-06-11T03:23:14.981Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Persistent state: `.criteria_results.json`\n\nThe repo holds a `.criteria_results.json` at its root.  Every\ncriterion script writes/updates its entry there on every run.  The\nschema is:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mkfs_timing\":     { \"status\": \"PASS\", \"last_run_iso\": \"...\", \"measured\": \"639ms\", \"threshold\": \"<=10000ms\", \"reason\": \"\" },\n  \"zero_silent_loss\":{ \"status\": \"FAIL\", \"last_run_iso\": \"...\", \"measured\": \"...\", \"threshold\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\" }\n}\n```\n\nThis is the model's **source of truth across sessions**.  On a fresh\nsession, before doing anything, run:\n\n```bash\n./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh --status\n```\n\nThis prints the current state of every criterion (from the JSON\nfile) without re-running anything.  Use it to:\n\n- See what's currently failing.\n- Pick the next failing criterion to work on.\n- Avoid re-running already-passing criteria mid-iteration.\n\nWhen a criterion script runs, it overwrites its own entry — so the\nfile always reflects each criterion's most-recent run.\n\n**Important:** `--status` shows the *last* result per criterion, which\nmay come from different runs.  The ship gate requires all criteria\nPASS in ONE end-to-end `verify_ship.sh` run (step 4 above).\n\n## Threshold rule\n\nThresholds reflect what the workload *should* take given the\narchitecture, not arbitrary caps.  If single-node rsync is 4s, 2-node\nparallel rsync should be ≈ 4s ± small constant.  If a verifier\nroutinely fails because the work is much slower than expected, fix\nthe FS — don't widen the threshold.\n\nCommon args for every verifier: `--nodes N` (count or comma list of\nhostnames), `--module PATH`, `--device DEV`, `--mount PATH`.  Defaults\ntarget the test17-test32 / `/dev/sda` / `/mnt/shared` cluster.\n\n---\n\n## CORRECTNESS (non-negotiable)\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| POSIX semantics preserved on every operation, from every node, under every concurrency pattern. | `tests/criteria/posix_semantics.sh --nodes 16` |\n| Zero silent data loss and zero silent dirent loss under any workload. | `tests/criteria/zero_silent_loss.sh --iters 3 --dpn 100 --mode 1` |\n| Crash consistency: acknowledged writes (post-fsync, post-close) survive any node death or power loss. | `tests/criteria/crash_consistency.sh --nodes 2` |\n| Cluster membership changes (join, leave, fence, recover) cannot lose data. | `tests/criteria/fence_during_write.sh --nodes 4` |\n| No false ENOENT/EEXIST under concurrent access — cache coherency is correct. | `tests/criteria/cache_coherency.sh --nodes 4` |\n| Strong consistency for fsync'd writes across nodes: a reader on node B sees them as soon as writer on node A's fsync returns. | `tests/criteria/strong_consistency.sh --nodes 4` |\n\n## SCALE\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| 16-node concurrent active R/W mount as the baseline target. | `tests/criteria/posix_semantics.sh --nodes 16` (covers it; cluster phase requires all 16 mounted) |\n| Surviving nodes continue uninterrupted after any single-node fence or death; automatic journal replay. | `tests/criteria/fence_during_write.sh --nodes 4` |\n| Workload doesn't degrade pathologically as nodes are added (no quadratic-cost ops). | `tests/criteria/scaling_curve.sh --nodes 16` |\n\n## PERFORMANCE — must be near-native XFS\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| Single-node mxfs operations within **≤ 5%** of native XFS on the same LUN (rsync as the canonical workload). | `tests/criteria/single_node_paired.sh --nodes 1` |\n| N-node aggregate throughput scales with N for embarrassingly-parallel workloads (independent files/dirs across nodes). | `tests/criteria/scaling_curve.sh --nodes 16` |\n| Canonical N-node rsync bench: per-node mxfs wall ≤ 1.2× single-node XFS reference. | `tests/criteria/rsync_paired.sh --nodes 4 --iters 1` |\n| Cluster ops (mount, unmount) complete in **seconds**, not minutes. | `tests/criteria/cluster_ops_timing.sh --nodes 4` |\n| No routine workload takes >2× the single-node XFS time. | Covered by `single_node_paired.sh` (single) and `rsync_paired.sh` (multi-node). |\n\n**Removed bullet:** \"Shared-resource contention within an order of\nmagnitude of GFS2/OCFS2.\"  We have no apples-to-apples GFS2/OCFS2\ntestbed here.  Shared-dir contention is instead bounded by\n`zero_silent_loss.sh`'s wall ceiling — any per-iter wall > a few","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
