{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P3Yju2u8rVxhnZZmRH7ZpX","type":"tool_result","content":"`zero_silent_loss.sh`'s wall ceiling — any per-iter wall > a few\nminutes on the workload-A storm is treated as structural breakage.\n\n## REAL WORKLOADS\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| Existing test framework passes clean: `tests/single/`, `tests/cluster/`, `tests/stress/`. | `tests/criteria/posix_semantics.sh --nodes 16` (wraps `run_tests.sh --phase all`) |\n| Canonical workload-A mkdir storm: 16-node × 100 dpn × ≥ 3 iters, 0 silent dirent loss. | `tests/criteria/zero_silent_loss.sh --iters 3` |\n| Canonical rsync bench: `rsync -a /root/open-gpu-kernel-modules/ <mxfs-mount>/<node>/` runs without corruption, aggregate scales near-linearly. | `tests/criteria/rsync_paired.sh --nodes 4` |\n\nPer-iter wall ceiling: anything > 5 minutes on these workloads is a\nstructural break, not overhead — diagnose, don't paper over.\n\n## ROBUSTNESS\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| No wedged unmounts requiring sysrq-b or `virsh destroy`. | `tests/criteria/wedged_unmount.sh --nodes 4` |\n| No kernel BUG/oops/panic on any documented operation. | `tests/criteria/dmesg_clean.sh --nodes 4` |\n| Continuous run under random-workload mix: no leaks, no growing caches, no fence storms. | `tests/criteria/soak.sh --nodes 4` (default 1h; set `SOAK_HOURS=24` for pre-ship) |\n| DLM/inode/block/dir cache caps honored — bounded memory. | `tests/criteria/cache_caps.sh --nodes 1` |\n\n## TOOLING\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| `mkfs.mxfs` completes in seconds for typical LUNs. | `tests/criteria/mkfs_timing.sh --nodes 1` |\n| `chk_mxfs` validates a healthy FS with zero false positives. | `tests/criteria/chk_clean.sh --nodes 2` |\n| Resize (grow): `resize_mxfs` claims new device space; prior data preserved. | `tests/criteria/online_resize.sh --nodes 1` (NOTE: current implementation is offline — script skips with reason if `mkfs_mxfs --size` is unavailable) |\n| Online add/remove node (mount/unmount while peers stay online). | `tests/criteria/online_membership.sh --nodes 3` |\n| DKMS clean install/uninstall. | `tests/criteria/dkms_install.sh --nodes 1` |\n\n---\n\n## Running the gate\n\n```bash\n# The ship gate — runs every criterion, stops at first FAIL\n./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh\n# Exit 0 = SHIP_GATE: PASS.  Exit nonzero = keep working.\n\n# Survey mode: don't stop at first FAIL.  Useful for \"what's broken\n# right now\"; never use as a ship sign-off.\n./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh --keep-going\n\n# Include the 1-hour soak (otherwise gated by SOAK_HOURS env)\n./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh --include-soak\n```\n\n## Running an individual verifier (debugging)\n\n```bash\n# Single criterion\n./tests/criteria/single_node_paired.sh --nodes 1\n\n# Look at the RESULT line\n$ ./tests/criteria/mkfs_timing.sh --nodes 1\nRESULT: PASS  criterion=mkfs_timing  measured=2480ms  threshold=<=10000ms\n\n# Failed run","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd05e5a4-1bae-4b40-b8b4-ee58800ac150","uuid":"5d1d1d3e-f75d-49a4-b719-90335a9a05ac","timestamp":"2026-06-11T03:40:35.771Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"`zero_silent_loss.sh`'s wall ceiling — any per-iter wall > a few\nminutes on the workload-A storm is treated as structural breakage.\n\n## REAL WORKLOADS\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| Existing test framework passes clean: `tests/single/`, `tests/cluster/`, `tests/stress/`. | `tests/criteria/posix_semantics.sh --nodes 16` (wraps `run_tests.sh --phase all`) |\n| Canonical workload-A mkdir storm: 16-node × 100 dpn × ≥ 3 iters, 0 silent dirent loss. | `tests/criteria/zero_silent_loss.sh --iters 3` |\n| Canonical rsync bench: `rsync -a /root/open-gpu-kernel-modules/ <mxfs-mount>/<node>/` runs without corruption, aggregate scales near-linearly. | `tests/criteria/rsync_paired.sh --nodes 4` |\n\nPer-iter wall ceiling: anything > 5 minutes on these workloads is a\nstructural break, not overhead — diagnose, don't paper over.\n\n## ROBUSTNESS\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| No wedged unmounts requiring sysrq-b or `virsh destroy`. | `tests/criteria/wedged_unmount.sh --nodes 4` |\n| No kernel BUG/oops/panic on any documented operation. | `tests/criteria/dmesg_clean.sh --nodes 4` |\n| Continuous run under random-workload mix: no leaks, no growing caches, no fence storms. | `tests/criteria/soak.sh --nodes 4` (default 1h; set `SOAK_HOURS=24` for pre-ship) |\n| DLM/inode/block/dir cache caps honored — bounded memory. | `tests/criteria/cache_caps.sh --nodes 1` |\n\n## TOOLING\n\n| Criterion | Verifier |\n|---|---|\n| `mkfs.mxfs` completes in seconds for typical LUNs. | `tests/criteria/mkfs_timing.sh --nodes 1` |\n| `chk_mxfs` validates a healthy FS with zero false positives. | `tests/criteria/chk_clean.sh --nodes 2` |\n| Resize (grow): `resize_mxfs` claims new device space; prior data preserved. | `tests/criteria/online_resize.sh --nodes 1` (NOTE: current implementation is offline — script skips with reason if `mkfs_mxfs --size` is unavailable) |\n| Online add/remove node (mount/unmount while peers stay online). | `tests/criteria/online_membership.sh --nodes 3` |\n| DKMS clean install/uninstall. | `tests/criteria/dkms_install.sh --nodes 1` |\n\n---\n\n## Running the gate\n\n```bash\n# The ship gate — runs every criterion, stops at first FAIL\n./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh\n# Exit 0 = SHIP_GATE: PASS.  Exit nonzero = keep working.\n\n# Survey mode: don't stop at first FAIL.  Useful for \"what's broken\n# right now\"; never use as a ship sign-off.\n./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh --keep-going\n\n# Include the 1-hour soak (otherwise gated by SOAK_HOURS env)\n./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh --include-soak\n```\n\n## Running an individual verifier (debugging)\n\n```bash\n# Single criterion\n./tests/criteria/single_node_paired.sh --nodes 1\n\n# Look at the RESULT line\n$ ./tests/criteria/mkfs_timing.sh --nodes 1\nRESULT: PASS  criterion=mkfs_timing  measured=2480ms  threshold=<=10000ms\n\n# Failed run","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
